        "title": "IngestAccepted",
        "description": "Response body. 202, because durability is all that is promised here.\n\nCounts are what was accepted for writing, not what was newly inserted -\nduplicates from a retry are accepted and silently deduplicated, and the\nclient must not treat a lower number as an error."
      },
      "IngestBatch": {
        "properties": {
          "traces": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/IngestTrace"
            },
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 1000,
            "title": "Traces"
          },
          "observations": {
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/IngestObservation"
            },
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 10000,
            "title": "Observations"
          },
          "sdk_version": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Sdk Version"
          }
        },
        "type": "object",
        "title": "IngestBatch",
        "description": "The POST /v1/ingest request body. Two envelopes are accepted.\n\nFlat (what the Python SDK sends), a single stream discriminated by `type`::\n\n    {\"events\": [{\"id\": ..., \"type\": \"trace\", ...},\n                {\"id\": ..., \"type\": \"generation\", \"trace_id\": ..., ...}]}\n\nNested, where observations are carried inside their trace::\n\n    {\"traces\": [{\"id\": ..., \"observations\": [...]}]}\n\nThe flat form is the one that suits a buffering client: spans finish\nindependently and flush in whatever order they complete, so requiring the\nnesting would force the SDK to hold a trace open until its last child\nreturned - and a long-running trace could not be reported until it ended.\nNothing is lost by accepting it, because every observation carries its own\ntrace_id and the router already creates a placeholder for a trace it has not\nseen yet.\n\nBoth normalise to the same internal shape before the router runs: `traces`\nfor trace rows, `observations` for the flat remainder."
      },
